{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "46a08782-e194-847a-95ba-0d80af9e45ff",
  "created_at": "2026-03-04T13:38:32-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Finance",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Nadia Patel",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Janet Whitcomb",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:34:52-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City of Newport Finance Department, this is Janet Whitcomb. How may I direct your call?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:34:58-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, I'm calling about my property tax bill. I've got you on speaker, I'm sorry, I'm in the shop and my hands are full. Can you hear me okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:35:09-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you. Go ahead. May I have your name and the property address, please?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:35:16-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nadia Patel. The address is 434 Pelham Street, up on the Hill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:35:21-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Ms. Patel. One moment while I pull up the account. [pause] All right, I have it. What is your question?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:35:30-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The bill went up from last year and I want to know why. It's quite a bit higher, and I didn't do anything to the building. No work, nothing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:35:41-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There are a few common reasons. The tax rate itself can change from year to year, and the assessed value may have been adjusted in a revaluation. Either of those would change the amount due even without any work on the property."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:35:56-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So how would I know which one it was? The rate or the value?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:36:02-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Your bill should list the assessed value and the rate. If you compare those figures to last year's bill, you will see which one moved. Do you have both bills in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:36:15-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I have this year's. Last year's is in the old, um, the old post office box, no, the file cabinet. Sorry. I'm thinking of where we used to keep things."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:36:26-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That is fine. If you read me the assessed value on this year's bill, I can tell you what is on record for the prior year."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:36:36-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hang on. [pause] It says the building assessment is, hold on, the speaker is cutting out. [line breaks up] Can you still hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:36:45-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I can hear you. Please continue."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:36:48-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Total assessed is four hundred eighty-one thousand two hundred."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:36:52-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. The prior year on file shows a lower total, so the assessed value did increase. That would account for part of the change in your bill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:37:03-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. That makes sense, I guess. And is there an exemption I can apply for? I've heard there are some."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:37:11-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There are several exemptions, depending on the circumstances. Which one are you asking about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:37:17-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The one for, well, I'm a business owner and I live above the shop. So I'd want the homestead one, if that's a thing. Is there a form number I should ask for?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:37:29-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Exemption applications are handled through the Assessor's office, and the forms vary by type. I do not want to give you the wrong number. I can transfer you there, or take your name and number and have them call you back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:37:44-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A callback is better. My number is 401-555-0169."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:37:48-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-zero-one, five-five-five, zero-one-six-nine. Is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:37:51-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. Oh, and actually, can you give me the Assessor's direct number too? My grandchild set up my new phone and I can't find the contacts in it. Everything moved."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:38:03-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm not able to read a direct line from this desk right now, but the Assessor's office is listed on the City of Newport website under the department directory. They will also be calling you, so you will have the number from your caller ID."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:38:19-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. I'll look at the website too. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:38:23-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You are welcome, Ms. Patel. I will send the request over this afternoon. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-04T13:38:30-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
